---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { SITE, CONTACTS } from '../config';

/**
 * DELETE ACCOUNT PAGE RULES — do not relax these when editing.
 *
 * 1. Required by Google Play's Data Safety "Data deletion" policy. Play
 *    reviewers open this URL directly, so it must stay public, indexable, and
 *    free of any login wall or redirect. Do not add noindex.
 * 2. Both routes to deletion stay on the page — in-app and by email. Play
 *    requires a route that does not depend on installing the app.
 * 3. Every retention claim here must match /privacy, which is the controlling
 *    document. Change one, change both.
 * 4. Recordkeeping guidance only. This page never tells anyone how long their
 *    own records need to be kept.
 */
const DELETION_MAILTO = `mailto:${CONTACTS.privacy}?subject=Delete%20My%20Account`;
---
<Prose
  title="Delete Your CabSnap Account"
  description="How to delete your CabSnap account and associated data."
  path="/delete-account"
  heading="Delete Your CabSnap Account"
  updated="August 14, 2026"
>
  <p>
    CabSnap (package name: {SITE.packageId}) is published by {SITE.company}. This page
    explains how to delete your CabSnap account and what happens to your data when you
    do. No login is required to read this page or to submit a deletion request.
  </p>

  <h2>Before you delete — export your receipts</h2>
  <p>
    Your receipts are business recordkeeping documents. Once your account is deleted,
    they cannot be recovered. If you may need them later, export or back them up from
    the app before requesting deletion. CabSnap provides recordkeeping tools only and
    does not provide tax advice — check with your own tax professional about how long
    you need to keep records.
  </p>

  <h2>Option 1 — Delete from inside the app (fastest)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open CabSnap on your Android device.</li>
    <li>Go to <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Tap <strong>Delete Account</strong>.</li>
    <li>Confirm. Your account and cloud-stored data are queued for permanent deletion.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Option 2 — Request deletion by email</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.privacy}`}>{CONTACTS.privacy}</a> from the email
    address on your CabSnap account, with the subject line "Delete My Account". Include
    the email address associated with your account so we can verify the request. We will
    confirm receipt and complete the deletion within 30 days. We may ask you to verify
    ownership of the account before we proceed.
  </p>

  {/* Wrapped in .cta so the button takes the same 360px desktop cap as every
      other primary action on the site, rather than stretching the column. */}
  <div class="cta">
    <a class="btn" href={DELETION_MAILTO}>Email a deletion request</a>
  </div>

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your account and login credentials</li>
    <li>Your profile information (name, email address)</li>
    <li>All receipt images stored in your CabSnap cloud account</li>
    <li>All extracted receipt data (merchant, date, amount, category, notes)</li>
    <li>Any organization or Fleet membership records tied to your account</li>
    <li>Your subscription record within CabSnap</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is retained, and for how long</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Residual copies may persist in encrypted system backups for up to 90 days after
      deletion, after which they are permanently overwritten.
    </li>
    <li>
      Records we are required to keep by law — such as payment and transaction records
      tied to a purchase — are retained for the period required by applicable law and
      tax regulations. These are held by our payment processor, not in your CabSnap
      account.
    </li>
    <li>
      De-identified, aggregated usage statistics that cannot be linked back to you or
      your device may be retained.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data stored only on your device</h2>
  <p>
    If you use CabSnap on the Free tier, your receipts are stored locally on your device
    and are never uploaded to our servers. Uninstalling the app removes that local data.
    Deleting your account does not affect data that only ever existed on your phone, and
    we cannot delete local data remotely.
  </p>

  <h2>Subscriptions</h2>
  <p>
    Deleting your CabSnap account does not automatically cancel a Google Play
    subscription. Cancel your subscription separately through the Google Play Store:
    Play Store → Profile icon → Payments &amp; subscriptions → Subscriptions → CabSnap →
    Cancel.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    Contact <a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.privacy}`}>{CONTACTS.privacy}</a>.
    {' '}{SITE.company}.
  </p>
</Prose>
